This project builds on the following third-party work:

- Laya multilingual (convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual) and the `laya` Python package — base model and
  fine-tuning tool for Jerzyk. Apache License 2.0. https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
- mmBERT-base (jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base) — multilingual encoder inside Laya multilingual. MIT License.
- Bielik 11B v3.0 Instruct (speakleash/Bielik-11B-v3.0-Instruct), SpeakLeash & ACK Cyfronet AGH — wrote the
  generated court / administrative / accounting test documents and filtered the training data. Apache License 2.0.
- Qwen3 8B (Qwen/Qwen3-8B), Alibaba Cloud — wrote the generated training documents. Apache License 2.0.
- llama.cpp — local inference of Bielik and Qwen during data preparation. MIT License.

Data sources:

- SAOS — System Analizy Orzeczeń Sądowych (https://www.saos.org.pl): real, already anonymised Polish court
  rulings. Court rulings are official documents and are not subject to copyright (art. 4 of the Polish
  Copyright Act).
- samorzad.gov.pl — public notices of Polish municipal, county and state offices. Official documents
  (art. 4 of the Polish Copyright Act); personal data of natural persons was replaced with [OSOBA] / [ADRES]
  before publication.
- The customer e-mails in the jerzyk-bench test and dev splits were written with Claude (Anthropic) for
  evaluation only. They were not used to train Jerzyk.

